cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "Erdos289: a Lean 4 development towards Erdős problem 289"
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 / mathlib development of a universal graded affine-correction
  theorem and its descent towards the strengthened length-{2,3} form of
  Erdős problem 289.  The universal core and five isolated hard leaves are
  proved unconditionally; the unconditional final theorem is not yet claimed.
authors:
  - family-names: Tang
    given-names: Yuren
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Yuren-Tang/erdos-289"
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - mathlib
  - formalization
  - Egyptian fractions
  - unit fractions
  - Erdős problems
references:
  - type: generic
    title: "Erdős problem 289"
    url: "https://www.erdosproblems.com/289"
